<section class="container my-5 article position-relative">
  
  <div class="testimonial-wrapper">
    <div class="slick fade-slide">
      <div>
        <div class="testimonial-excerpt"><p>&ldquo;I can&rsquo;t even put into words the wonderful experience I had at Pellissippi State. I went to Germany through the study abroad program and got involved with lots of organizations. Pellissippi was the best option for me and for anyone interested in transferring to a larger school.&rdquo;</p></div>
        <p class="testimonial-name">Abbey Becker</p>
        <p class="testimonial-title">Communications and Marketing Specialist, Oak Ridge Institute for Science and Education</p>
      </div>
      
      <div>
  <div class="testimonial-excerpt"><p>&ldquo;I&rsquo;m so grateful for my experience at Pellissippi State. The smaller class size, great teachers and supportive environment helped me to transition into college. And I graduated without any debt.&rdquo;</p></div>
  <p class="testimonial-name">Amelea Everett</p>
  <p class="testimonial-title">Community Relations Analyst with the Knoxville Utility Board</p>
</div>
      
      <div>
  <div class="testimonial-excerpt"><p>&ldquo;I took dual enrollment classes at Pellissippi State then transferred with the help of Tennessee Promise. So I basically went to school for free. I didn&rsquo;t want to jump into a university and was drawn to the smaller campus. At Pellissippi I made a lot of friends and the professors were very understanding."</p></div>
  <p class="testimonial-name">Carlissa Weeks</p>
  <p class="testimonial-title">Director of Emerald Academy (a college preparatory school)</p>
</div>
      
      
      
      
      
    </div>
  </div>
</section><span id="d.en.13384"></span>
